VALUES ('software-architecture-fundamentals', 'Software Architecture Fundamentals: Modules, Dependencies & When to Split a Service', 'Learn the architecture decisions you make every week without calling them that: modules, layers and services, coupling and cohesion, which way dependencies point, ports for payment and email, refactoring without changing behaviour, and deciding between a modular monolith and microservices with evidence.', 'A beginner course for developers who have built a small application and now wonder why every change touches five files. Every lesson starts from a situation on the CodeDev learning platform - an OrderService that grew to 900 lines and talks to the database, email and payment directly, a refactor that sent the receipt email before the payment was confirmed, an AI-generated refactor that made two modules import each other, a team that wanted microservices because the monolith felt slow - and answers it with a decision you can check: modules, layers and services, coupling and cohesion measured as fan-in and fan-out, dependency direction, ports and adapters, refactoring behind tests, the Monolith or Microservices scenario, shared databases, the signals that justify splitting a service, and architecture decision records. 10 lessons with True/False quizzes on real code and situations, and TypeScript challenges graded by hidden tests.', 'https://res.cloudinary.com/dex6q1cqh/image/upload/c_limit,w_1600/f_auto,q_auto/v1793023867/codedev/courses/software-architecture-fundamentals/cover', 'beginner'::level_enum, 240, 'CodeDev Engineering Team', 0, 0, 50,
