2026-10-24 14:02  build codedev-api@a91f3c2 -> 1 image  api:a91f3c2
2026-10-24 14:06  rollout api:a91f3c2 to 3 instances  OK

Statement: "orders and payments are separate modules here but not separate services: a fix in payments reaches production only by deploying the whole API, and the call from orders to charge() is an ordinary function call inside one process, not a network request."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. There is one build and one image, so every module ships in the same deploy, and the import resolves to a function in the same Node.js process: no HTTP, no serialisation, no timeout between orders and payments (charge() may still call Stripe over the network, but that is a different boundary). This is a modular monolith: boundaries in the code, one deployable. The misconception is that folders per feature already make services; what makes a service is a separate deploy and a network call between the parts, with the costs that come with them.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_saf_111') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
