module          fanIn  fanOut  instability
utils               9       0         0.00
catalog             3       2         0.40
payments            2       2         0.50
notifications       2       1         0.33
orders              1       5         0.83
progress            1       3         0.75

Statement: "utils has an instability of 0.00, so it is the safest module to change: nothing it depends on can break it."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Instability = fanOut / (fanIn + fanOut). A value of 0 means the module depends on nothing and many modules depend on it: it will rarely be broken by others, but every change to it reaches all 9 importers, which is exactly what happened. "Stable" in this metric means hard to change safely, not safe to change. A module like this needs a small, deliberate API and tests that cover its callers before any edit; orders (0.83) is the one that can change cheaply, because only 1 module depends on it. The misconception is reading "stable" as "low risk".', 1, 5
