The proposal: replace utils with three modules, money (formatPrice), email (sendEmail) and levels (calculateLevel); formatDate and slugify move to a small text module.

Statement: "After this split, a change to calculateLevel can break progress and leaderboard, but it can no longer break catalog or orders."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. After the split, only progress and leaderboard import levels, so a change to calculateLevel reaches exactly those two; catalog and orders import money and text, which did not change. Each new module is also more cohesive: everything in it changes for the same reason (pricing rules, email delivery, the level formula). Before the split, every importer of utils depended on all five functions at once, so any edit touched all of them. The misconception is that splitting a module only moves code around: it changes who depends on what, which is what decides how far a change spreads.', 2, 5
