VALUES ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_saf_122'), 1, 'Fan-in counts distinct importers, not import lines. What data structure keeps one entry per importer even when the same edge appears three times with different spacing?'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_saf_122'), 2, 'Work in three passes: parse and validate each line (split on "->", trim both sides, check the number of parts and that no name is empty or contains whitespace), record the module names and the edges, then build one report row per module and sort. The self-edge check comes after a module has been recorded, not before.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_saf_122'), 3, 'A similar graph: "lessons -> media", "quizzes->media", "lessons -> media", "media -> cdn", "cdn -> cdn", "media cdn". One line is invalid (skipped 1). media is imported by lessons and quizzes (fanIn 2) and imports cdn (fanOut 1): instability = Math.round(100 / 3) / 100 = 0.33. cdn: fanIn 1, fanOut 0, instability 0. lessons and quizzes: fanIn 0, fanOut 1, instability 1. Order: media, cdn, then lessons before quizzes.');
