/src/modules/progress/        @codedev/platform-team
# platform-team: 6 developers, one sprint board, one on-call rotation
# One Postgres database. Code that reads the orders table:
#   src/modules/orders/, src/modules/payments/, src/modules/progress/report.ts

Evidence B - deploy pipeline, last 30 days:
Pipeline deploy-production: 19 runs, 17 succeeded, 2 failed, median 20m 10s
Median step durations
  install dependencies          1m 40s
  lint + typecheck              2m 05s
  test (unit + integration)    12m 30s   1 worker, test files run one after another
  build                         1m 55s
  migrate database              0m 40s
  rollout (2 instances)         1m 20s
Failed runs
  2026-09-30  rollout  health check failed in src/modules/progress/report.ts:
              ERROR: column o.amount does not exist
              (migration 0412 renamed orders.amount to orders.amount_vnd) - rolled back
  2026-10-03  migrate  ERROR: canceling statement due to lock timeout
              (migration 0412b on orders waited behind checkout transactions, lock_timeout 5s)

Statement: "Both failed deploys last month came from one change to the orders table, a table that code in three modules reads directly."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. In B the first failure is the rename in migration 0412 breaking a query in src/modules/progress/report.ts, and the second is the reworked migration 0412b on the same orders table waiting behind checkout transactions. A lists orders, payments and progress/report.ts as code that reads orders directly. So the deploy failures come from a table shared by several modules, not from the amount of code in one deployable. The common misconception is to read every failed deploy as proof that "the monolith is too big"; the evidence points at shared data, which a split does not remove unless the data is split too.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_saf_311') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
