Evidence D - RFC-031 "Split the platform into microservices":
Services (7): catalog, orders, payments, notifications, progress, users, leaderboard
Each service: own repository, own pipeline, own database; HTTP calls and events between them
Expected benefits: "deploys get fast because each service is small",
                   "catalog can scale on its own",
                   "a bug in one service cannot break the others"

Statement: "Splitting the app into the seven services of RFC-031 would by itself bring deploys well under 20 minutes, because each service would deploy less code."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. B shows that 12m 30s of the 20 minutes is the test step running on one worker. Seven pipelines would each still install, lint, test, build and roll out, and nothing in the RFC changes how tests run. The direct fix for this evidence is to run tests in parallel and, on pull requests, only the tests of the changed modules, which works in one repository today. The misconception is that deploy time grows with the size of the codebase; it grows with the slowest step, and you find that step in the pipeline, not in the architecture diagram.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_saf_311') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
