37 receipts sent for declined payments, 12 learners got course access without paying
Trace of one checkout (order o_51873)
10:14:02.104  orders         placeOrder o_51873 course=redis-patterns amount=149000
10:14:02.106  orders         email.sendReceipt -> POST notifications/receipts o_51873
10:14:02.131  notifications  receipt queued for hoa.tran@example.com o_51873
10:14:02.133  orders         events.publish order.paid o_51873
10:14:02.140  progress       grantAccess u_9310 redis-patterns (consumer of order.paid)
10:14:02.902  orders         payments.charge o_51873 -> declined (insufficient_funds)
10:14:02.910  orders         orders.save o_51873 payment_failed
PR #611, first hunk of placeOrder:
+    // notifications is its own service now: tell it as early as possible
+    deps.email.sendReceipt(order.learnerEmail, order.id, order.amountVnd);
+    deps.events.publish("order.paid", { orderId: order.id, learnerId: order.learnerId, courseId: order.courseId });
     const result = deps.payments.charge(order.id, order.amountVnd);

Statement: "The receipts went out for declined cards because placeOrder sends the receipt and publishes order.paid before it calls charge; the same code would do the same with notifications still a module in the same process."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The trace shows the sending side''s own order: sendReceipt at .106, publish order.paid at .133, charge at .902. Nothing was reordered by the network; orders sent the side effects first, and the diff shows the lines that moved them there. The extraction was the motive ("tell it as early as possible") but not the mechanism: an in-process EmailSender called first would send the same wrong receipt, and an in-process progress module listening for order.paid would grant the same access. The misconception is to blame distribution or eventual consistency for a bug that is plain call order in one function.', 4, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_saf_311') AND order_index = 4)
    RETURNING id
)
