    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_saf_341'), 'docs/adr/ in October 2027:
0007-keep-a-modular-monolith.md   Status: Superseded by 0012 (text unchanged since 2026-10-16)
0012-extract-payments-service.md  Status: Accepted
  Context: trigger 1 of ADR 0007 fired - a payments team of 4 was formed in August 2027
           and owns src/modules/payments; ...

Statement: "Keeping the text of ADR 0007 and marking it as superseded by ADR 0012 is the intended way to change a decision recorded in an ADR."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. An ADR records a decision made at a point in time with what was known then; it is not edited to match a later decision. The old record changes only its status and points to the new one, and the new record explains which trigger fired and why the answer changed. Both stay in the repository, next to the code, so the history of the decision is reviewable like any other change. The misconception is to rewrite the old ADR in place, which erases the reasoning that was right at the time and makes it look as if the team never decided otherwise.', 3, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_saf_341') AND order_index = 3)
    RETURNING id
